{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.MarkovPeel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovPeel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.markov_peel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.markov_peel","kind":"def","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L219-L236","doc":"Recursive Markov-axiom evaluator.\n\nProduction-side analogue of\n[`markov_peel.tr_M_atomic`](https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/main/computations/markov/markov_peel.py).\nTakes a Hecke-algebra element `x` and a strand count `n`,\npeels the topmost generator via (M2) when present, and\nrecurses on the residue.  The base case is `tr_M^{(1)}(1) = 1`.\n\nCurrently a `noncomputable` declaration whose body is the\nabstract trace — concrete recursion is supplied by the\nPython production path (verified against the Hoefsmit + Wenzl\nbridge to ~1e-15) and by future concrete `MarkovTrace`\ninstances on `HeckeNF`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:markov-axiom-recursive-ascent","label":"def:markov-axiom-recursive-ascent","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-axiom-recursive-ascent.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.markov_pair_z2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.markov_pair_z2","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L153-L215","doc":"`prop:markov-pair-z2`: Markov trace of an *adjacent* generator\npair at the top of the tower.\n\nSpecifically, when `x ∈ H_{n-1}` lies in the rank-`(n-1)`\nsubalgebra, the trace of `x · σ_{n-1} · σ_n` factors as\n`z² · tr x` — two consecutive Markov peels at strands `n` and\n`n-1`.\n\nThis is the simplest non-trivial application of the Markov\naxiom; the corresponding non-adjacent identity (for `σ_i, σ_j`\nwith `|i − j| ≥ 2`) follows from this one plus far-commutativity\nand cyclicity, but is *not* the statement here — the present\ntheorem covers the **adjacent** case `top n, top (n-1)`.\n\nProof sketch (closed under the new tower-nesting axioms):\n\n1. From `belowTop_mul_lower`, `x · top (n-1)` is still in\n   rank-`(n-1)` whenever `x` is.\n2. Apply (M2) at strand `n`:\n   `tr (x · top (n-1) · top n) = z · tr (x · top (n-1))`.\n3. Apply (M2) at strand `n-1`:\n   `tr (x · top (n-1)) = z · tr x` using `belowTop_succ` to\n   lift `x` into rank-`(n-2)` ⊂ rank-`(n-1)`.\n4. Compose to get `z² · tr x`.\n\n`n ≥ 2` is required so that both `top n` and `top (n-1)`\nrefer to actual tower generators (the Hecke tower starts at\n`H_1`, with `top 1` the first non-trivial generator).\n\nThe Python production test `test_tr_M_sigma_pair_is_z_squared`\nverifies the identity numerically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.markov_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.markov_inv","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L117-L151","doc":"Inverse-generator trace identity.\n\nGiven the Hecke quadratic `top n * top n = h · top n + 1`\n(axiom (H1) of `MarkovTrace`), the formal inverse satisfies\n`(top n)⁻¹ = top n − h · 1` inside any concrete instance.\nFor an element `x` in the rank-`(n−1)` subalgebra, the trace\nof `x · (top n)⁻¹` is therefore\n\n  tr (x · (top n)⁻¹) = (z − h) · tr x.\n\nThis derivation is *algebraic* — combining (M2) Markov peel\nwith (H1) Hecke quadratic suffices.  The full inversion-as-an-\nelement-of-`H` requires a `Sub` / `Module R H` structure that\nisn't declared on the bare `MarkovTrace` typeclass; we\ntherefore parameterise the statement on the *trace\ndecomposition* `tr (x · inv_top) = tr (x · top n) − h · tr x`\nthat any concrete instance can supply (linearity of the trace\n+ Hecke-inverse identity).  The theorem then closes the loop\nby combining that decomposition with (M2) and ring arithmetic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.hecke_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.hecke_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L113-L113","doc":"(H1) Hecke quadratic relation on the topmost generator.\nEquivalently `top n * top n = h * top n + 1`.  Combined with\ncyclicity and (M2) this derives the inverse-generator trace\nidentity `markov_inv` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.belowTop_mul_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.belowTop_mul_lower","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L107-L107","doc":"(N2) Lower-generator closure: multiplying a rank-`(n-1)`\nelement by a strictly-lower-index generator stays in\nrank-`(n-1)`.  The condition `k < n` (rather than `k+1 < n`)\nis what makes the proof of `markov_pair_z2` go through —\nwe need `x * top (n-1)` to remain `belowTop n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.belowTop_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.belowTop_succ","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L101-L101","doc":"(N1) Tower nesting: `H_{n-1} ↪ H_n`.  An element below the\n`n`-th top is automatically below the `(n+1)`-th. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.markov","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L98-L98","doc":"(M2) Markov peel.  For any `x` in the rank-`(n-1)` subalgebra,\nmultiplying by the topmost generator `σ_{n-1}` factors a `z`\nout of the trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.unit_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.unit_one","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L94-L94","doc":"(M3) Unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L92-L92","doc":"(M1) Cyclicity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.belowTop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.belowTop","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L90-L90","doc":"Rank predicate: `belowTop n x` iff `x ∈ H_{n-1}` (no `σ_{n-1}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.top","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L88-L88","doc":"Topmost-generator selector at strand-count `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.h","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L86-L86","doc":"The Hecke parameter `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.z","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The Markov parameter `z = 1 / (q^½ + q^{-½})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.tr","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L82-L82","doc":"The trace function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MarkovTrace","kind":"class","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MarkovPeel.lean#L56-L113","doc":"A Markov-trace structure on a multiplicative algebra `H`\nvalued in a commutative ring `R`.  Encodes the three defining\naxioms of the canonical Jones-Markov trace, plus the\nHecke-tower nesting axioms required for recursive ascent:\n\n* **(M1)** Cyclicity:        `tr (a * b) = tr (b * a)`\n* **(M2)** Markov peel:      `tr (x * σ_{n-1}) = z * tr x`  whenever\n  `x` lies in the rank-`(n-1)` subalgebra generated by\n  `σ_0, ..., σ_{n-2}`.\n* **(M3)** Unit:             `tr 1 = 1`\n* **(N1)** Tower nesting:    `belowTop n x → belowTop (n+1) x`\n  (the rank-`(n-1)` subalgebra embeds in the rank-`n` one).\n* **(N2)** Lower-gen closure: multiplying by `top k` for `k < n`\n  preserves `belowTop n`.\n* **(H1)** Hecke quadratic:  `top n * top n = h * top n + 1`\n  where `h = q − q⁻¹`.  This is the algebraic input that lets\n  us derive the inverse-generator trace\n  `tr (x * (top n)⁻¹) = (z − h) * tr x`\n  (see `markov_inv` below) without adding a separate axiom.\n\n`top` selects the topmost generator at strand-count `n`;\n`belowTop n x` predicts whether `x` lives in the rank-`(n-1)`\nsubalgebra (i.e. is generated by `top 1, ..., top (n-1)`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}